   "id": "ex1",
   "type": "example",
   "title": {
    "en": "Complete dissolution"
   },
   "problem": {
    "en": "A and B share 3:2. Balance sheet: Creditors ₹30,000, Bills Payable ₹10,000, General Reserve ₹10,000, Capitals A ₹60,000, B ₹40,000 (total ₹1,50,000); Cash ₹15,000, Debtors ₹35,000, Stock ₹40,000, Machinery ₹60,000 (total ₹1,50,000). Debtors realise ₹33,000; A takes stock at ₹36,000; machinery sells for ₹55,000; creditors are paid ₹29,000; bills payable paid in full; expenses ₹2,000. Prepare the accounts."
   },
   "steps": [
    {
     "en": "Realisation Dr: assets 1,35,000 + creditors paid 29,000 + B/P 10,000 + expenses 2,000 = ₹1,76,000."
